# §B2 fixture coverage gate (added in #18). The Tier B2 lift in #17
# (commit 57c2ba1) collapsed weapon_off / armor_off / weapon_ready /
# armor_ready in src/subs.c into two-line trampolines into the
# subs.equipment.{unequip,equip} DSL scripts. None of the 44 pre-#18
# fixtures exercised the P / T / W / R wilderness keystrokes that
# route through those scripts, so the lift's runtime behaviour was
# validated by code review only.
#
# Smallest viable coverage: weapon_off on a fresh-party member with
# no weapon (early-return path). Sequence after party create is
# `P` (weapon_off keystroke) + `1` (slot 1 / member A) + `X` + `Y`
# (quit). Members A..D from the create-party setup all have weapon=0
# under seed 42, so the dispatcher hits the
# `cond: { eq: [{ member: ..., field: 'weapon' }, 0] }` branch,
# emits subs.equipment.no_weapon, pauses 800ms (RYL_NO_DELAY=1
# elides the wall-clock delay), then clw + return. Exercises the
# resolve_field_name DSL extension (#17, 5c082f1) end-to-end:
# `field: { var: 'kind' }` resolves to 'weapon' via the trampoline's
# kind binding, then routes into pm_field_table's weapon row.
RYL_FAKE_EPOCH=1700000000
RYL_FAKE_SEED=42
RYL_NO_DELAY=1
